# PART 3 — INVESTIGATE EXISTING IMPLEMENTATION GAPS

Investigate these initial concerns against the complete codebase.

## 3.1 Authentication

Inspect AuthGate.tsx, App.tsx and the Python authentication implementation.

Determine:

- Whether Google OAuth is real.
- Whether authenticated users can be forged by changing frontend state.
- Whether the backend validates identity.
- Whether sessions are secure.
- Whether logout invalidates the real session.
- Whether any fixed user identity is present.
- Whether user data leaks between sessions.

Do not consider a frontend button that sets authenticated=true to be authentication.

## 3.2 Gemini API integration

Inspect all Gemini integrations.

Determine:

- Whether the frontend calls Gemini directly.
- Whether the backend calls Gemini.
- Which model identifiers are configured.
- How API keys are stored.
- Whether placeholder credentials exist.
- Whether fallback responses are simulated.
- Whether error handling is accurate.
- Whether API limits are respected.

Never expose a Gemini API key in the frontend production bundle.

BYOK implementation must have a documented threat model and must not falsely claim that a client-side secret is protected from the client.

## 3.3 Hook-generation implementation

Investigate the difference between:

- Actual transcript-based analysis.
- Title-based Gemini prompts.
- Hardcoded fallback templates.
- Synthetic timestamps.
- Actual generated subtitles.

A hook must never be represented as transcript-verified unless it has been validated against source content.

Test timestamps against actual video duration and transcript timing.

## 3.4 Video preview

Inspect actual media sources and preview state.

Determine whether playback is:

- Genuine source video playback.
- Timestamp-based source playback.
- Simulated playback.
- A mock preview.

Verify switching videos and hook cards does not introduce stale state.

## 3.5 Video export

Inspect the complete chain:

Frontend → request → backend → yt-dlp → FFmpeg → Whisper → ASS generation → final MP4 → download.

Determine which functions are connected and which are only simulated.

Do not mark export complete when only a timer or progress indicator has finished.

